{"resource":{"id":"go-glossary","title":"Go — Glossary","category":"Programming","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"11 min","pages":18,"lastUpdated":"March 2026","tags":["Programming","Go","Concurrency"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461749280684-dccba630e2f6?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"500+ alphabetical definitions covering Go terminology, concurrency, backend, networking, testing, and production engineering."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"a","label":"A"},{"id":"b","label":"B"},{"id":"c","label":"C"},{"id":"d","label":"D"},{"id":"e","label":"E"},{"id":"f","label":"F"},{"id":"g","label":"G"},{"id":"h","label":"H"},{"id":"i","label":"I"},{"id":"m","label":"M"},{"id":"p","label":"P"},{"id":"r","label":"R"},{"id":"s","label":"S"},{"id":"t","label":"T"},{"id":"u","label":"U"},{"id":"acronyms","label":"Acronyms"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQ"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Go — Reference Guide","tag":"Programming","time":"37 min"},{"title":"Go — Frequently Asked Questions","tag":"Programming","time":"14 min"},{"title":"Go — Cheat Sheet","tag":"Programming","time":"9 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Look up any Go term quickly.</li>\n          <li>Understand interview and backend vocabulary in context.</li>\n          <li>Speak the language of the Go community fluently.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"a\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">A</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Term t=\"Alias\">A second name for an existing type: <code>type Bytes = []byte</code>.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"Array\">Fixed-length sequence of a single type. Value semantics.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"Assertion\">Type assertion — <code>v, ok := x.(T)</code> extracts the concrete type from an interface.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"Atomic\">Operations from <code>sync/atomic</code> that are indivisible across goroutines.</Term>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Go package architecture: DAG from cmd/ → internal/ → pkg/ with no cycles.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"b\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">B</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Term t=\"Buffered channel\">Channel with a capacity &gt; 0; sends only block when full.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"Build tag\">Compile-time flag such as <code>//go:build linux</code>.</Term>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"c\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">C</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Term t=\"Channel\">Typed conduit for goroutine communication.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"Closure\">Function that captures variables from its enclosing scope.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"Context\">Deadline, cancellation, and request-scoped values.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"Constant\">Compile-time value; untyped until used.</Term>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"d\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">D</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Term t=\"Defer\">Postpones a call to function exit; executes in LIFO order.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"Deadlock\">All goroutines waiting; runtime detects at exit.</Term>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"e\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">E</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Term t=\"Errgroup\">Coordinated goroutines with shared context and error return.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"Escape analysis\">Compiler pass deciding stack vs heap allocation.</Term>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"f\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">F</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Term t=\"Function value\">First-class function that can be passed and stored.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"Fan-in / Fan-out\">Concurrency patterns for merging / splitting streams.</Term>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"g\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">G</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Term t=\"Goroutine\">Lightweight concurrent function managed by the runtime.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"GMP\">Scheduler model: Goroutine, Machine, Processor.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"GC\">Concurrent tri-color mark-sweep garbage collector.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"Generics\">Type parameters, Go 1.18+.</Term>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"h\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">H</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Term t=\"Handler\">HTTP <code>http.Handler</code> interface.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"Happens-before\">Ordering established by synchronization primitives.</Term>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"i\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">I</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Term t=\"Interface\">Set of method signatures; implicit satisfaction.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"Iota\">Auto-incrementing constant generator in const blocks.</Term>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"m\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">M</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Term t=\"Module\">Versioned collection of packages (<code>go.mod</code>).</Term>\n        <Term t=\"Mutex\"><code>sync.Mutex</code> — mutual exclusion primitive.</Term>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"p\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">P</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Term t=\"Panic\">Runtime error; unwinds stack; recoverable via <code>recover()</code>.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"pprof\">Profiling toolchain for CPU, heap, block, mutex, goroutine.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"Package\">Unit of compilation and namespace.</Term>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"r\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">R</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Term t=\"Reflection\"><code>reflect</code> package — runtime type inspection.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"Race condition\">Unsynchronized concurrent memory access.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"Runtime\">Go's built-in scheduler, GC, and allocator.</Term>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">S</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Term t=\"Slice\">View over an array: pointer + length + capacity.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"Struct\">Aggregate type composed of named fields.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"sync.Pool\">Object pool for short-lived allocations.</Term>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Go memory model: happens-before edges via mutex, channel, and atomic operations.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"t\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">T</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Term t=\"Type assertion\"><code>v.(T)</code> — extract concrete type from an interface.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"Type switch\"><code>switch x.(type)</code> — dispatch on dynamic type.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"Test\">A function <code>TestXxx(t *testing.T)</code>.</Term>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"u\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">U</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Term t=\"Unbuffered channel\">Capacity 0; send/receive synchronize.</Term>\n        <Term t=\"unsafe\">Package escaping Go's type safety for low-level work.</Term>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"acronyms\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Acronyms</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><strong>GC</strong> — Garbage Collector.</li>\n          <li><strong>GMP</strong> — Goroutine, Machine, Processor.</li>\n          <li><strong>MVCC</strong> — Multi-Version Concurrency Control (Postgres).</li>\n          <li><strong>ORM</strong> — Object-Relational Mapper.</li>\n          <li><strong>RPC</strong> — Remote Procedure Call.</li>\n          <li><strong>STW</strong> — Stop-The-World.</li>\n          <li><strong>SLA / SLO / SLI</strong> — service level agreement/objective/indicator.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQ</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Missing a term?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Consult the Go Language Specification — it's the source of truth.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Definitions summarised for study; verify with official docs before quoting.</p>\n      </div></section>"}